        "pitfall": "Never aggressively hyperventilate a chronically hypercapnic patient (e.g. COPD baseline PaCO2 60) down to a normal PaCO2 of 40 mmHg in the ICU or post-op. Rapid normalization of PaCO2 against high retained bicarbonate causes severe post-hypercapnic metabolic alkalosis, seizures, arrhythmias, and weaning failure.",
