        "b": "Correct size selection is the single most critical determinant of clinical success with the i-gel. Unlike inflatable LMAs where cuff volume can be adjusted post-insertion, the i-gel relies on exact anatomical matching of its non-inflatable cuff to the patient's laryngeal framework. Sizing is strictly weight-based and color-coded across seven distinct sizes spanning neonates to large adults:\n\n• Size 1 (Pink): Neonate, 2 to 5 kg. Has no gastric channel due to microscopic lumen dimensions.\n• Size 1.5 (Light Blue): Infant, 5 to 12 kg. Accommodates up to 10 Fr NG tube.\n• Size 2 (Grey): Small paediatric, 10 to 25 kg. Accommodates up to 10 Fr NG tube.\n• Size 2.5 (White): Large paediatric, 25 to 35 kg. Accommodates up to 12 Fr NG tube.\n• Size 3 (Yellow): Small adult, 30 to 60 kg. Accommodates up to 12 Fr NG tube.\n• Size 4 (Green): Medium adult, 50 to 90 kg. Accommodates up to 12 Fr NG tube.\n• Size 5 (Orange): Large adult, 90+ kg. Accommodates up to 14 Fr NG tube.\n\nWhen a patient's weight sits on the borderline between two sizes (e.g., exactly 50 kg or 90 kg), clinical guidelines recommend selecting the smaller size if the patient has a slender neck, recessed chin, or narrow palate, and the larger size if the patient has a wide muscular neck or broad facial features.",
